# Auto-deploy GAS after changes

When you change backend or shared app sources (`Code.js`, `JavaScript.html`, `CSS.html`, `Index.html`, `LoginShell.html`, `appsscript.json`) and the user wants the fix live (or says deploy / push / ship):

1. Run `npm run build:pages` if front-end sources changed.
2. Run `npm run deploy:gas` to `clasp push` and redeploy the production web app.
3. Commit and push to `master` when the user asked to publish (GitHub Pages deploys via Actions).

Do not skip GAS deploy after pushing app changes — GitHub Pages alone is not enough; the API must be redeployed too.
